          "channel_id": "1519311669216673802",
          "components": [],
          "content": "**@everyone | Newsroom Update: Deconstructing the Oil Volatility Spike**\n\nWe've just published a data-driven briefing analyzing the recent surge in WTI crude volatility and its implications for US recession models.\n\n**The Hard Numbers (as of June 29, 2026):**\n* **WTI Spot Price:** $71.87/bbl (up 7.8% from $66.66 on Feb 19, 2026)\n* **1-Year Change:** +4.6% (from $68.73 on June 12, 2025)\n* **Volatility Proxy:** 30-day absolute daily moves averaged 2.8%, representing a **50.7% increase** in realized volatility over the last 90 days.\n\n**Why this matters:** Rising energy volatility widens the range of macro outcomes, complicating inflation progress and narrowing consumer spending cushions. However, we caution against fusing this lazily with yield-curve signals.\n\nCheck out the channel #macro-briefings or click the link to read our full methodology and source trail: https://capitalchronicle.substack.com/p/crude-awakening-how-spiking-oil-volatility-4f7",
